1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Listen to a talk in an art history class.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:02,401
Woman:

3
00:00:02,401 --> 00:00:11,200
Expressionism is an influential modernist art movement that emerged in the early 20th century.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:19,230
This movement is characterized by its focus on representing emotional experience rather than physical reality.

5
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:25,794
Expressionist artists aim to convey their inner feelings and perceptions through distorted

6
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:28,564
and exaggerated forms, vivid colors,

7
00:00:28,564 --> 00:00:30,190
and bold brush strokes.

8
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:36,287
One of the most famous expressionist artists is Edvard Munch.

9
00:00:36,287 --> 00:00:41,040
His painting The Scream shows an agonized person crying out.

10
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:47,170
It eventually became an icon of the movement's focus on intense personal experience.

11
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:56,240
Expressionism was not limited to visual arts, however — it also influenced the literary, theater, and cinematic arts.

12
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:02,234
In literature, authors like Franz Kafka explored themes of alienation

13
00:01:02,234 --> 00:01:07,030
and existential angst in his bizarre, dreamlike fiction.

14
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:15,350
Expressionist theater often used dramatic lighting and intense performances to evoke emotional responses.

15
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:19,190
Sets sometimes featured oversized symbolic objects.

16
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:27,014
In Elmer Rice's 1923 play The Adding Machine, a giant adding machine represents the

17
00:01:27,014 --> 00:01:29,250
dehumanizing forces of technology.

18
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:36,232
Similarly, the German Expressionist film movement used innovative techniques such as cutting between scenes

19
00:01:36,232 --> 00:01:41,220
with a shared sound to help create emotionally charged narratives.

20
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:47,813
Despite its impact, expressionism faced criticism for its departure from traditional aesthetics

21
00:01:47,813 --> 00:01:51,110
and its emphasis on the personal.

22
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:56,999
Critics argued that its focus on subjective emotion robbed the works of broader content

23
00:01:56,999 --> 00:01:57,840
or meaning,

24
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:04,150
and the bold brushwork in paintings was sometimes viewed as lacking in skill and technique.

25
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:10,811
Nonetheless, expressionism paved the way for later movements, such as surrealism, leaving a lasting

26
00:02:10,811 --> 00:02:13,190
legacy in the art world.
